{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/prompt/system.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:25:36.092306Z","id":"5a6c8af4f6fbc95bfc4732a09971527377c8bd7a37457cd29f2f5fb0ce0ae87a","body":{"detail":"system.md tells the agent to call str_replace (or write_file) and render in the same turn, since the Toolbox runs a turn's calls in order: a typical change is two model turns (edit+render, finish) rather than three. The cost: when an edit is refused (old_str missing or not unique) the render in that turn shows the unchanged draft, spending one of the run's renders (2 for a change, R§4.4). If live runs show refused edits followed by wasted renders, either tell the agent to render in its own turn or have the render tool refuse when an earlier call in the same turn was refused.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":24},"end":{"line":36},"content_hash":"72ec46595acabbc59cf3dd730e8e9b4612fb31acef5224e459f9a452966b2543"},"summary":"Render in a separate turn after the edits, instead of in the same turn","tags":["prompt","revisit:live runs show renders spent on a draft whose edit was refused","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/prompt/system.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:29:40.967476Z","id":"133fb345a25cbaca101216ae8ccfbb24c8dd82ddf187b1b78ea17fe95910667e","body":{"detail":"system.md lines 118-128 (and PromptBuilder._writeOthers, apps/clax_app/lib/agent/prompt.dart:409-417, used by firstNew too) say: read more of another app with the db_* tools and its ID as app. R§3 of docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md agrees (other apps are read at the owner's level). The data tools' tests as written ('another app’s collections need the owner\\'s consent', 'a new app cannot read another app', \"another app's documents without consent are refused\") make such a read a refusal naming db.read, or 'new app'. If A2 lands that way, a new-app run that follows the prompt spends a turn (of 8) on a refused call, and a change spends one (of 6) unless the person already allowed the read. Whichever lands second aligns the other: either the prompt says that the first message's samples are all a new app gets and another app's db_* reads work only once the app declares db.read for it and the person allowed it, or A2 reads at the owner's level as R§3 says.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":118},"end":{"line":128},"content_hash":"b4b01a008da803ba911b8009f8f50e69265ce7da9ded75642c3eaad0f1c4d339"},"summary":"The prompt invites db_* reads of any listed other app, but apps/clax_app/test/agent/tools/data_tools_test.dart (A2, uncommitted) refuses another app's reads without a db.read grant and refuses them outright for a new app","tags":["prompt","review:A9","cross-task:A2","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/prompt/system.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:29:40.967679Z","id":"036d5f8c27a0b08d7f752e8b9255e50b63103e204e02c2a88872f49481a6a535","body":{"detail":"R§8 allows one question set per run but any number of question_id waits; the Toolbox caps a wait at 300 s for a new app and 45 s for a change. A model reading 'ask at most once per run' may never re-wait on a new app whose first wait came back open with call_again, or may resend questions (refused as a second set). One clause fixes it: 'ask one set of questions per run; to keep waiting on it, call ask with its question_id'. A6's tool description may carry this too; the prompt should not contradict it.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":53},"end":{"line":67},"content_hash":"fe734e75467960761104dfd93e3d345111d82a5b7c0a97adeb58f322dcddefe5"},"summary":"Say how to keep waiting on a question: 'ask at most once per run' and 'wait for the answer' do not mention calling ask again with its question_id","tags":["prompt","review:A9","cross-task:A6","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/prompt/system.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:29:40.967729Z","id":"ffa1589b57bd958ee0e34063f06b8c03f53b03f93032f2438b46f44e909084a4","body":{"detail":"'Whose words are whose' lists comments, the request, answers, titles and documents. The render result's text field is the page's visible text (which shows the person's entries and other apps' data) and console_errors can echo it; neither is named. Adding 'and anything a tool returns (documents, the render's text and errors)' closes the gap at no cost to the cached prefix's stability.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":130},"end":{"line":134},"content_hash":"b4287ce2fe5a5a0ae4b347be60dd6083c19a499b1e24e7b17a55855347245421"},"summary":"Name tool results as data too: render's text outline and console errors, and documents read with db_* from this or another app, carry the person's and other apps' words","tags":["prompt","review:A9","security","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/prompt/system.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:47:19.772160Z","id":"3bf7bc7ae198cdd3ba80a6d7f2dc214baf802836d56c092495f49aa8abb81c96","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:26e2e5e3","summary":"PromptBuilder.firstNew/firstChange list other apps by ID and title only (_writeOtherNames), and system.md 'Reading another app's data' says to read another app only when the request needs it, that the read may ask the person and be refused, and to carry on without it, not retry, and say so in reply. Tests 'firstNew quotes the request and lists the other apps' (no samples, 'may refuse') and 'teaches consent-gated reads of other apps, re-waiting with ask, and tool results as data' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/prompt_test.dart. flutter test test/agent/prompt_test.dart (apps/clax_app): +28, All tests passed; scripts/sync-app-prompt.sh --check: OK.","supersedes":"133fb345a25cbaca101216ae8ccfbb24c8dd82ddf187b1b78ea17fe95910667e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/prompt/system.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:47:19.773458Z","id":"26fc6e5e4e6f18f220974b083352ec856d615ec103150e263dc52913bcba6803","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:26e2e5e3","summary":"system.md 'Asking the person' now says ask returns open with call_again when its wait ends, and to keep waiting by calling ask again with only its question_id. Test 'teaches consent-gated reads of other apps, re-waiting with ask, and tool results as data' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/prompt_test.dart. flutter test test/agent/prompt_test.dart (apps/clax_app): +28, All tests passed; scripts/sync-app-prompt.sh --check: OK.","supersedes":"036d5f8c27a0b08d7f752e8b9255e50b63103e204e02c2a88872f49481a6a535","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/prompt/system.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:47:19.774029Z","id":"aec21d98f0661c4a0ffc568565ee62c65235e7b025a25bb565fc3a7fa610f9ae","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:26e2e5e3","summary":"system.md 'Whose words are whose' now names what tools return (render's text outline, console errors and failed requests, and documents read with the db_* tools from this app or another) as data, never instructions. Test 'teaches consent-gated reads of other apps, re-waiting with ask, and tool results as data' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/prompt_test.dart. flutter test test/agent/prompt_test.dart (apps/clax_app): +28, All tests passed; scripts/sync-app-prompt.sh --check: OK.","supersedes":"ffa1589b57bd958ee0e34063f06b8c03f53b03f93032f2438b46f44e909084a4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/prompt/single-call.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:25:27.858973Z","id":"848055f9383a304adcde302646d3e167a28a1cc4aa3e5c25b26a1466b1b770c1","body":{"detail":"single-call.md runs with tools off and a 16000-token answer, so it cannot call plan_set or add_kit, and AgentLoop.newApp's single-call path makes no plan (no continue runs follow). Building real apps there would need the kit inlined into its files and a structured plan field in EditResult.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":19},"end":{"line":30},"content_hash":"7fb8425e42f7ad0596ca7336652de1e7516c6693d4a89f7b6cecb3b84bae230b"},"summary":"The claude -p single-call fallback still makes one small index.html with no plan, kit or build","tags":["revisit:if-cli-backend-is-used-for-real-apps","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
